{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210692,"nonce":"Lkhc1Bsbz5c7slPV8cFEdSVMXJw=","title":"AOT fibers: krio-fiber backing is opt-in; stackless state-machine transform remains the default","message":"WLIFT_KRIO_FIBER=1 attaches a krio_fiber::Fiber to each ObjFiber (src/runtime/core/fiber.rs) and Fiber.yield switches synchronously. Default off. The default AOT path is still transform_to_state_machine driven by compute_aot_tainted_method_names (src/codegen/aot.rs).\n\nTwo suspension paths that do not compose:\n- Mechanism A (SM-poll): tainted bodies become poll functions with a br_table prologue; suspension is return-from-function. Correct.\n- Mechanism B (native FiberAction::Yield arm in runtime_fns.rs handle_jit_fiber_action): returns the value with no state change or unwinding. Cannot work from inside an AOT body and must never fire there.\n\nCracks where B leaks: Fn.call(_) on a closure is dynamic, so the taint set has to include every call(N) site if any closure yields (currently gated behind WLIFT_AOT_CALL_N; without it hatch/site spins in app.listen); the taint walk only sees Instruction::Call, so any new native primitive that yields breaks the invariant silently.\n\n- Drop the SM transform, BlockKind, aot_frames, aot_active_depth and the taint analysis once every AOT spec passes with WLIFT_KRIO_FIBER=1.\n- Open risks recorded before integration: GC (fiber stacks must be walked as roots; krio_jit_roots snapshot exists), re-entrancy (nested resume through native frames), lifetime (Box\u003cFiber\u003e pinned while ObjFiber moves).\n- Compare against the state-machine path on the hatch spec corpus (41 specs) and hatch/site before flipping.","files":null}]}